WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.130
In Santiago, a viewer turns on the
subtitles of your product video,

2
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.230
and every line is English.

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.350
The video has one subtitle file,
and every cue in it is English.

4
00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.300
General Translation translates the text

5
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:19.770
in SRT subtitle files and
keeps every timestamp.

6
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:26.010
Install gt, then list the
subtitle files in gt.config.json,

7
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.130
with one folder per locale.

8
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:31.130
Sign in, add your project ID,

9
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.470
and run npx gt translate for
the Spanish and French files.

10
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.750
Each new file keeps the timing lines and
cue numbers, and only the words change.

11
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.470
In Santiago, the player
loads the new files,

12
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.750
and the same cue reads
in French or Spanish.
